  {%- comment -%}
    All Google Fonts in one request. They used to be pulled in by 38 separate CSS
    @import lines inside individual sections, which is the slowest way to load a
    font: the browser cannot see them until it has parsed that CSS, they cannot be
    preloaded, and the same family was fetched several times at different weights
    (Chivo five ways, Inter four). Preconnect first so the TLS handshake to both
    Google hosts overlaps the HTML parse.
  {%- endcomment -%}
